    "https://www.bates.edu/purposeful-work/handshake/": {
      "title": "Center for Purposeful WorkOpportunities and Programs",
      "description": "Handshake Internship/Job Search Platform | Center for Purposeful Work | Bates College Menu Search Admission Visit Campus Visit Virtually Student Financial Services Academics Calendar Course Catalog Resources Campus Dining Menu Events Map Alumni Alumni Directory Events Reunion Arts Athletics New Students Library News Parents & Families Strategic Planning About Us Purposeful Work College Store Community-Engaged Learning Equity & Inclusion President Sustainability Support Bates The Quad Center for Purposeful Work Opportunities and Programs Page Menu Purpose Connect Where to Find Us Staff Team Make an Appointment Student Teams Purpose and Your Club PW Weekly Newsletters For Alumni and Parents In The News Media Professionals Media Inquiries Prepare Resume, Cover Letter, Interview & Networking Activities to Explore Purposeful Work Professional Development Opportunities Mini Grant Funding Request Form Life After Bates Explore Job Shadow Program Self Assessments Industry Roadshows Spotlights on Alumni Career Paths Purposeful Work Unplugged Curriculum Practitioner-Taught Courses Purposeful Work Infusion Project Faculty Resources for Purposeful Work Infusion Courses Life Architecture Short Term Course First-Year Seminar: Purpose, Work, and College Opportunities Handshake Internship/Job Search Platform Purposeful Work Internships For Employers: Recruiting at Bates For Students: Recruiting at Bates Employer Recruitment Session Schedule Micro-Internships Grants, Credit & Fellowships Industry Specifics STEM and Pre-Health Support & Resources Pre-Law Support & Resources Pre-Business Support & Resources Pre-Engineering Support & Resources Discover Entrepreneurship Application Deadlines by Industry Graduate Support Graduate School Support & Resources Graduate/Professional School Events Outcomes Postgraduation Survey for Class of 2026 Class of 2024 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2023 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2022 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2021 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2020 Post Graduation Outcomes Handshake Internship/Job Search Platform Handshake is Bates’ online tool for exploration, planning, research, and internship and job listings. Students and alumni can use the direct Bates link ( handshake.bates.edu ) to: create their individualized profiles, and share their skills and experiences with potential employers; join virtual events, and research internship and job opportunities; and access scores of resources through the Center for Purposeful Work (including Vault industry guides as well as resume, cover letter, interviewing, and networking guides). With listings from thousands of employers targeted at college students and recent graduates, including listings shared by alumni and parents, Handshake makes opportunities across industries available for all Bates students to access. Handshake Guide Log In to Handshake Website Disclaimer The Bates Center for Purposeful Work maintains its websites as a service to Bates students and alumni for their career development and job search efforts, but the presence of job announcements on any site maintained by the Bates Center for Purposeful Work does not indicate an endorsement or recommendation by Bates College or the Bates Center for Purposeful Work. Students and alumni are solely responsible for taking all necessary precautions when interviewing for or accepting internships or jobs, as well as checking the credentials and integrity of an employer or organization. Please refer to our recruiting expectations, guidelines, and policies for additional information. Schedule a Meeting with a Purposeful Work Counselor Students: To schedule an individual meeting, make an appointment via Handshake with a specific counselor or a counselor aligned with your needs and interests. 1. Log in to Handshake with your Bates email and SSO. 2. Go to Career Center (visible in multiple locations on the homepage). 3. Click Appointments . Once you see Schedule a New Appointment , follow the prompts. After you decide whom to meet with given your needs and interests, you have the option to select one of the following mediums: – Zoom: We’ll send a Google calendar invitation with a Zoom link. – Phone: Please provide a phone number in the Handshake notes where you articulate what we can help you with. We’ll send a Google calendar invitation and include that phone number. – In-Person Meeting: We’ll send a Google calendar invitation with a physical location. Once you’ve scheduled your appointment, check your email or Google Calendar for the meeting invitation detailing your counselor’s name as well as applicable meeting details. Alumni: You won’t be able to schedule via Handshake, so please email purposefulwork@bates.edu with your Monday-Friday availability, your preferred medium (see list above), and either the name of a specific counselor or your questions/needs/interests so we can connect you with an appropriate counselor. We should respond within 2-3 business days. Update Your Profile on Handshake to Make Sure It Reflects Your Skills and Experiences Recruiters will frequently review Handshake profiles to determine whether individuals are suitable for open roles. The more complete and updated your profile, the more likely recruiters will consider your candidacy for relevant roles. Log in to Handshake with your Bates email and SSO. Click on your initials or image in the upper right corner to open a drop down menu. Select My Profile. Complete each section. If you already have an updated resume, you can easily cut and paste into each section. Update Your Career Interests on Handshake to Receive Emails with Opportunities Targeted to Your Interests Log in to Handshake with your Bates email and SSO. Click on your initials or image in the upper right corner to open a drop down menu. Select My Career Interests. Complete each section, paying particular attention to the following: Which Bates College career clusters best match your interests? Which industries are you interested in? Which kinds of job, or job functions, interest you? When do you expect to graduate? Click Save in the lower right corner. Update Your Settings on Handshake to Make Sure Your Profile is Public and You Get the Notifications You Want Recruiters will only be able to reach out to you if you make your profile public and if you set your notifications accordingly. Log in to Handshake with your Bates email and SSO. Click on your initials or image in the upper right corner to open a drop down menu. Select Settings. Save Specific Search Criteria on Handshake and Receive Notifications of New Internships or Jobs that Fit Those Criteria This option can be really helpful when you’ve identified specific search criteria that filter for internships or jobs you want. By saving these search criteria on Handshake, the platform can notify you based on your notification preferences (see above) whenever new internships or jobs get posted that fit these search criteria. This option will make the search process a lot more efficient. CONSIDER THIS EXAMPLE: Log in to Handshake with your Bates email and SSO. Click on Jobs on the left-hand side. Select All Filters on the horizontal filters bar (this will open a pop-up box). Under Job Type, select On-Campus. Click Show Results in the lower right corner of the pop-up box. You should now see all available On-Campus jobs that are open for application. On this Jobs screen, you’ll see a blue bar with a bell and a message that says “Notify me about new jobs like this.” If you toggle the switch from left to right, you’ll save the search. If you click “Manage notifications,” you’ll be taken to the Notification Preferences section discussed above. Handshake Resources Handshake Blog for Students Finding a Job on Handshake: FAQs How to Get the Best Job Recommendations from Handshake PW Quick Links Where We Are & Drop In Hours Schedule an Appointment Handshake RAIN Employer Info Session Schedule Cover Letter Guide Resume Guide Center for Purposeful Work Search these pages Bates Center for Purposeful Work 56 Campus Ave Chase Hall, Suite 101 Lewiston, Maine 04240 PHONE 1-207-786-6232 Email purposefulwork@bates.edu News & Updates September 4, 2026 AESOP trips encourage authenticity, connection The Class of 2030, the third largest in Bates history, gathered to kick off AESOP on Friday, Aug. 28 — the day after move-in day. September 4, 2026 Opening Convocation at Bates welcomes Class of 2030, encourag… The college welcomed the Class of 2030 and new transfer students to the official start of the new academic year at the Sept.  1 Convocation on the Historic Quad. September 4, 2026 Bates welcomes (more) new faculty Bates News began introducing new faculty last week and will continue over the next few weeks. Read our second installment below. Bates\n\t\t\t\t\tCollege 2 Andrews Road Lewiston, Maine 04240 Phone: 1-207-786-6255 Make a Gift Campus Safety Communications Directory Employment Sexual Respect / Title\n\t\t\t\t\t\tIX A-Z Index Privacy Policy Questions &\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFeedback Virtual Tour Previous Next"
    },
    "https://www.bates.edu/purposeful-work/other-opportunities/": {
      "title": "Center for Purposeful WorkOpportunities and Programs",
      "description": "Grants, Credit & Fellowships | Center for Purposeful Work | Bates College Menu Search Admission Visit Campus Visit Virtually Student Financial Services Academics Calendar Course Catalog Resources Campus Dining Menu Events Map Alumni Alumni Directory Events Reunion Arts Athletics New Students Library News Parents & Families Strategic Planning About Us Purposeful Work College Store Community-Engaged Learning Equity & Inclusion President Sustainability Support Bates The Quad Center for Purposeful Work Opportunities and Programs Page Menu Purpose Connect Where to Find Us Staff Team Make an Appointment Student Teams Purpose and Your Club PW Weekly Newsletters For Alumni and Parents In The News Media Professionals Media Inquiries Prepare Resume, Cover Letter, Interview & Networking Activities to Explore Purposeful Work Professional Development Opportunities Mini Grant Funding Request Form Life After Bates Explore Job Shadow Program Self Assessments Industry Roadshows Spotlights on Alumni Career Paths Purposeful Work Unplugged Curriculum Practitioner-Taught Courses Purposeful Work Infusion Project Faculty Resources for Purposeful Work Infusion Courses Life Architecture Short Term Course First-Year Seminar: Purpose, Work, and College Opportunities Handshake Internship/Job Search Platform Purposeful Work Internships For Employers: Recruiting at Bates For Students: Recruiting at Bates Employer Recruitment Session Schedule Micro-Internships Grants, Credit & Fellowships Industry Specifics STEM and Pre-Health Support & Resources Pre-Law Support & Resources Pre-Business Support & Resources Pre-Engineering Support & Resources Discover Entrepreneurship Application Deadlines by Industry Graduate Support Graduate School Support & Resources Graduate/Professional School Events Outcomes Postgraduation Survey for Class of 2026 Class of 2024 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2023 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2022 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2021 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2020 Post Graduation Outcomes Grants, Credit & Fellowships Internships, study abroad, conference travel, academic research – all are ways students take a thoughtful, concrete next step and test the hypothesis that they’ve formed about themselves based on their personalities, values, strengths and interests. The Center for Purposeful Work assist students in exploring and considering a wide variety of funded opportunities as a way to test their passions, build skills and knowledge, and gain exposure to the work that interests them. For students without inherited networks of professionals and mentors, gaining experience and contacts in a workplace opens doors to additional people on whom they can rely for guidance in their future. There are hundreds of paid and unpaid opportunities to experience work posted in Handshake including Purposeful Work Internships , Bates Environmental Internships , Innovate for Maine and the Hanley Health Internships . Funded Student Experiences Bates Academic Year & Summer Grants: Bates Student Research Grant STEM Travel Grant Hoffman Research Support Grant Bates Environmental Internships Harward Center Academic Year Grants Summer Funded Opportunities Summer Research Fellowship STEM Student – Faculty Summer Research Grant Internships for Credit If an employer requires “academic credit” for an internship, a student may apply for the Internship for Credit status. Through this program, one credit may be available as a notation on the student’s transcript. Please be aware that internship credit will not count as one of the 32 credits required for graduation, nor will it be included in a student’s GPA. Qualifications: Internships must last a minimum of six weeks and at least 120 hours. Internships for credit are reviewed by the Center for Purposeful Work on a semesterly basis. Students are limited to two qualifying internships for a total of two transcript notations. Note: This information does not apply to internships completed as part of a Bates course requirement. If you have questions about a specific course that requires the completion of an internship, or questions about designing an independent study, please contact the academic department or the Registrar’s Office. International students: Any international student who is applying for an internship for credit must also apply for CPT per the standard CPT process. Begin by contacting Shelley Palmer in Global Education. Although international students generally may not apply for CPT during their first year, they may apply for CPT for the summers of their sophomore or junior years.  Students may also participate in a CPT-authorized internship during their winter break, which is rare but does occasionally occur. Any CPT during the academic semester will affect the student’s post-completion OPT. Therefore: International students (F-1 Visa holders) are only eligible for internship-for-credit during the summers, specifically between their sophomore/junior and junior/senior summers International students are not eligible for academic year internships-for-credit unless careful consideration is made regarding the impact on their OPT and the time available for post-grad work in the United States. Deadlines: Applications for internship for credit are due by the following dates or two weeks before the internship begins, whichever comes first: Fall 2024 internships – October 22, 2024 Winter 2025 internships – February 18, 2025 Summer 2025 internships – July 15, 2025 For more information and application forms, please contact the Center for Purposeful Work at purposefulwork@bates.edu . Fellowships Bates College ranks fourth in the nation for Fulbright U.S. student awards. Students interested in applying for prominent nationally competitive awards such as the Fulbright, Rhodes and Watson should contact Dr. Robert Strong, Director of National Fellowships, at rstrong@bates.edu and visit the Graduate Fellowship Committee’s homepage . There are many other fellowships to which students and alumni can apply directly.  For questions and advice about fellowships please review the fellowship overview in the Resource section of Handshake or contact the Bates Center for Purposeful Work for advice about options. Immodest proposals:  Students offer tips for fellowship success PW Quick Links Where We Are & Drop In Hours Schedule an Appointment Handshake RAIN Employer Info Session Schedule Cover Letter Guide Resume Guide Center for Purposeful Work Search these pages Bates Center for Purposeful Work 56 Campus Ave Chase Hall, Suite 101 Lewiston, Maine 04240 PHONE 1-207-786-6232 Email purposefulwork@bates.edu News & Updates September 4, 2026 AESOP trips encourage authenticity, connection The Class of 2030, the third largest in Bates history, gathered to kick off AESOP on Friday, Aug. 28 — the day after move-in day. September 4, 2026 Opening Convocation at Bates welcomes Class of 2030, encourag… The college welcomed the Class of 2030 and new transfer students to the official start of the new academic year at the Sept.  1 Convocation on the Historic Quad. September 4, 2026 Bates welcomes (more) new faculty Bates News began introducing new faculty last week and will continue over the next few weeks. Read our second installment below. Bates\n\t\t\t\t\tCollege 2 Andrews Road Lewiston, Maine 04240 Phone: 1-207-786-6255 Make a Gift Campus Safety Communications Directory Employment Sexual Respect / Title\n\t\t\t\t\t\tIX A-Z Index Privacy Policy Questions &\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFeedback Virtual Tour Previous Next"
