      "title": "Where to Find Us",
      "description": "Where to Find Us | Center for Purposeful Work | Bates College Menu Search Admission Visit Campus Visit Virtually Student Financial Services Academics Calendar Course Catalog Resources Campus Dining Menu Events Map Alumni Alumni Directory Events Reunion Arts Athletics New Students Library News Parents & Families Strategic Planning About Us Purposeful Work College Store Community-Engaged Learning Equity & Inclusion President Sustainability Support Bates The Quad Center for Purposeful Work Opportunities and Programs Page Menu Purpose Connect Where to Find Us Staff Team Make an Appointment Student Teams Purpose and Your Club PW Weekly Newsletters For Alumni and Parents In The News Media Professionals Media Inquiries Prepare Resume, Cover Letter, Interview & Networking Activities to Explore Purposeful Work Professional Development Opportunities Mini Grant Funding Request Form Life After Bates Explore Job Shadow Program Self Assessments Industry Roadshows Spotlights on Alumni Career Paths Purposeful Work Unplugged Curriculum Practitioner-Taught Courses Purposeful Work Infusion Project Faculty Resources for Purposeful Work Infusion Courses Life Architecture Short Term Course First-Year Seminar: Purpose, Work, and College Opportunities Handshake Internship/Job Search Platform Purposeful Work Internships For Employers: Recruiting at Bates For Students: Recruiting at Bates Employer Recruitment Session Schedule Micro-Internships Grants, Credit & Fellowships Industry Specifics STEM and Pre-Health Support & Resources Pre-Law Support & Resources Pre-Business Support & Resources Pre-Engineering Support & Resources Discover Entrepreneurship Application Deadlines by Industry Graduate Support Graduate School Support & Resources Graduate/Professional School Events Outcomes Postgraduation Survey for Class of 2026 Class of 2024 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2023 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2022 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2021 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2020 Post Graduation Outcomes Student Affairs Center for Purposeful Work Connect Where to Find Us Where to Find Us batespurposefulwork Summer has officially started!!😎  Thank you to eve 🚨New summer campus resource unlocked 👀  The Bobcat ANNOUNCEMENT 📢  Purposeful Work is hiring!  Lookin Past pitches. Big ideas. Real impact.   Bobcat Ven Ever wondered what it’s really like to be a trial Welcome back from the PW team! ⭐️  Drop-Ins start There’s still time to apply for a Job Shadow! Subm Need a professional headshot taken TODAY?  Pass by Take advantage of this great weather and get a fre Take a look at how hard our Purposeful Work summer ATTENTION sophomores and juniors! 💼   Submit your Hey Bobcats! 🐾 We hope you had a chance to unwind Need a new professional headshot?  Stop by our fre Stressed about internship applications? PW is here 🚨PW INTERNSHIP PROGRAM DEADLINES APPROACHING🚨   So Drop by for a FREE headshot at Purposeful Work’s p Bates Summer Internship deadlines are coming up fa It’s internship season!! Make sure to stop by Chas Looking for a purposeful summer experience? ☀️ We’ Welcome to the new year and the winter semester! ❄ Load More Follow on Instagram General Information Our office hours are Monday through Friday, with occasional evening or weekend events, workshops, and employer info sessions (check Handshake for the latest schedule updates). Email us any time. If you have questions about our programs or need to reach us, send us an email at purposefulwork@bates.edu. Drop-Ins with our PW Peer Advisors are offered six days a week. Stop by without an appointment, during the day or evening hours. See details below. Document Reviews. While we prefer to meet with students individually (virtually or in-person), we can review application materials via email, if necessary. PLEASE NOTE: We can only review documents in MS Word or Google Docs formats. Documents submitted in other formats will be returned via email, with a request for a Word or Google Doc format, which may delay the review process. Need a quiet interview space? If you want to reserve an interview room for a phone/virtual interview, contact Purposeful Work at purposefulwork@bates.edu with your date and time request at least 2-3 days in advance. Interview rooms are located on the ground floor of Ladd Library. Students can reserve a room in Ladd through PW. Drop-In Hours No appointment necessary for Purposeful Work support! During the academic year, o ur student team of PW Peer Advisors are available to help with resumes, cover letters, LinkedIn profile reviews, and any questions about Purposeful Work programs. Just stop by! We are located in Chase Hall, First Floor, in the Purposeful Work Lobby Area. During the academic year, the PW Peer Advisors will be available during the following hours: Sundays: 7:00 – 9:00pm Mondays: 1:30 – 3:30pm and 7:00 – 9:00pm Tuesdays: 1:30 – 3:30pm and 7:00 – 9:00pm Wednesdays: 1:30 – 3:30pm and 7:00 – 9:00pm Thursdays: 1:30 – 3:30pm Fridays: 1:30 – 3:30pm Please note: Drop-In Hours are only offered while classes are in session. There are no drop-in hours during academic breaks. Where We Are Our staff team meets with students in person on campus as well as remotely. Because of variable schedules, it’s best to make appointments with us on Handshake or by emailing purposefulwork@bates.edu . Starting with the Fall Semester 2023, you can find the Center for Purposeful Work on the first floor of Chase Hall along with the Student Center for Belonging and Community, Residential Life, Student Activities, Campus Life, and more. Chase Hall entrance on Campus Ave : This is the most accessible entrance for mobility. Enter these doors and take the elevator straight ahead to the first floor. Turn right into the lobby and the Purposeful Work Suite. Chase Hall entrance on Ladd-Carnegie-Chase Plaza : This door is up one flight of stairs. Enter Chase here, go through the vestibule, and turn right just beyond the couch. The Purposeful Work Suite will be straight ahead. PW Quick Links Where We Are & Drop In Hours Schedule an Appointment Handshake RAIN Employer Info Session Schedule Cover Letter Guide Resume Guide Center for Purposeful Work Search these pages Bates Center for Purposeful Work 56 Campus Ave Chase Hall, Suite 101 Lewiston, Maine 04240 PHONE 1-207-786-6232 Email purposefulwork@bates.edu News & Updates September 4, 2026 AESOP trips encourage authenticity, connection The Class of 2030, the third largest in Bates history, gathered to kick off AESOP on Friday, Aug. 28 — the day after move-in day. September 4, 2026 Opening Convocation at Bates welcomes Class of 2030, encourag… The college welcomed the Class of 2030 and new transfer students to the official start of the new academic year at the Sept.  1 Convocation on the Historic Quad. September 4, 2026 Bates welcomes (more) new faculty Bates News began introducing new faculty last week and will continue over the next few weeks. Read our second installment below. Bates\n\t\t\t\t\tCollege 2 Andrews Road Lewiston, Maine 04240 Phone: 1-207-786-6255 Make a Gift Campus Safety Communications Directory Employment Sexual Respect / Title\n\t\t\t\t\t\tIX A-Z Index Privacy Policy Questions &\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFeedback Virtual Tour Previous Next"
