utcomes Class of 2020 Post Graduation Outcomes Student Affairs Center for Purposeful Work Connect Purpose and Your Club Purpose and Your Club You’re in a club for a reason. Maybe you’re interested in the content or activities, maybe you’re deeply aligned with the club’s mission. Maybe you want to make connections with like-minded people, or maybe you just joined to have fun. Whatever the reason, there’s a purpose behind your membership. We can help you explore your purpose, maybe uncovering more connections than you realize! In your club, you’re learning and utilizing skills that have real-world applicability. We’re here to help you articulate those skills and incorporate your experience into your personal story so you can leverage them in a cover letter, resume, interview, or alumni connection. Contact purposefulwork@bates.edu to learn more about how we can help enhance your experience as well as the experience of your club! Club Collaboration – We can help you: Bring in Speakers – We can help you make alumni connections and bring relevant speakers to talk to your clubs Add Club Experience To Your Resume – We can help you articulate the value of your leadership or membership in your club to help you stand out in a resume, cover letter or interview! Define Transferable, Career-Related Skills – We can help analyze and define your skills and the ways in which they transfer to the “real world.” Craft Workshops or Make Individual Appointments – We offer workshops as well as individual appointments. Contact us to plan a visit with your club or set up an appointment for yourself! PW Quick Links Where We Are & Drop In Hours Schedule an Appointment Handshake RAIN Employer Info Session Schedule Cover Letter Guide Resume Guide Center for Purposeful Work Search these pages Bates Center for Purposeful Work 56 Campus Ave Chase Hall, Suite 101 Lewiston, Maine 04240 PHONE 1-207-786-6232 Email purposefulwork@bates.edu News & Updates September 4, 2026 AESOP trips encourage authentic