Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2020 Post Graduation Outcomes Student Affairs Center for Purposeful Work Prepare Professional Development Opportunities Professional Development Opportunities Wall Street Prep – Finance Preparation (discounted access) Rocket Blocks – Consulting & Tech Interview Preparation (discounted access) CaseQuestions – Consulting Case Interview Preparation (free access) To access all session and workshop recordings, sign in here with your Bates email. Investure – Investment Management with Client Schools Skill-Building, Networking, and Landing an Internship at an Investment Firm ​ – 9/14, 6-7PM Careers in Investing; Endowment Investing 101 – 9/16, 6-7PM Management Consulted (limited seats available – please ONLY register if you can attend the ENTIRE workshop): Fall Workshop – 11/14, 10AM-1PM Breaking into Consulting from the Liberal Arts Winter Workshop – 2/20, 10AM-1PM Preparing for Case Interviews NOTE: If you can’t make these workshops, check out their website and explore their free resources. They offer free webinars regularly and their pages cover the workshop content and more. AESOP Academy (limited seats available – please ONLY register if you can attend the ENTIRE workshop): Fall Excel 1 – 9/19, 11AM-3:30PM Excel Basics Fall Excel 2 – 9/20, 11AM-3:30PM Excel Intermediate Fall Excel 3 – 9/26, 11AM-3PM Excel Empowerment (ideal for students who completed Excel 1&2 last year) Fall AI Prompting for Analyst Functions – 10/10, 11AM-3PM Fall Project Management – 11/7, 11AM-3:30PM (ideal for students working on academic projects, research projects, club/team projects & senior theses) Monthly Session: Getting Started with Business Interests – Consulting, Finance, Marketing & More (open to all classes) September Session – 9/21, 7:30-9PM October Session – 10/19, 7:30-9PM November Session – 11/16, 7:30-9PM Center for Purposeful Work Search these pages Bates Center for Purposeful Work 56 Campus Ave Chase Hall, Suite 101 Lewiston, Maine 04240 PHONE 1