      "description": "Purposeful Work Internships | Center for Purposeful Work | Bates College Menu Search Admission Visit Campus Visit Virtually Student Financial Services Academics Calendar Course Catalog Resources Campus Dining Menu Events Map Alumni Alumni Directory Events Reunion Arts Athletics New Students Library News Parents & Families Strategic Planning About Us Purposeful Work College Store Community-Engaged Learning Equity & Inclusion President Sustainability Support Bates The Quad Center for Purposeful Work Opportunities and Programs Page Menu Purpose Connect Where to Find Us Staff Team Make an Appointment Student Teams Purpose and Your Club PW Weekly Newsletters For Alumni and Parents In The News Media Professionals Media Inquiries Prepare Resume, Cover Letter, Interview & Networking Activities to Explore Purposeful Work Professional Development Opportunities Mini Grant Funding Request Form Life After Bates Explore Job Shadow Program Self Assessments Industry Roadshows Spotlights on Alumni Career Paths Purposeful Work Unplugged Curriculum Practitioner-Taught Courses Purposeful Work Infusion Project Faculty Resources for Purposeful Work Infusion Courses Life Architecture Short Term Course First-Year Seminar: Purpose, Work, and College Opportunities Handshake Internship/Job Search Platform Purposeful Work Internships For Employers: Recruiting at Bates For Students: Recruiting at Bates Employer Recruitment Session Schedule Micro-Internships Grants, Credit & Fellowships Industry Specifics STEM and Pre-Health Support & Resources Pre-Law Support & Resources Pre-Business Support & Resources Pre-Engineering Support & Resources Discover Entrepreneurship Application Deadlines by Industry Graduate Support Graduate School Support & Resources Graduate/Professional School Events Outcomes Postgraduation Survey for Class of 2026 Class of 2024 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2023 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2022 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2021 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2020 Post Graduation Outcomes Student Affairs Center for Purposeful Work Opportunities Purposeful Work Internships Purposeful Work Internships Looking for a summer internship? Start thinking about: what are you curious about, which skills would you like to work on this summer, what are your budgetary needs, whether you’d like to be in-person, remote, or hybrid, where you’d like to live, etc… As a starting point, check out: Bates Summer Funded Opportunities You can find more about all the funding sources at Bates for low or unpaid summer internships PW Employer Partner Program Through this program, employers provide strong mentorship, meaningful summer work, and opportunities to network across industry. Many more opportunities will be added weekly. Deadlines vary so check back often as this is updated on a rolling basis as soon as we receive confirmed details from our Employer Partners Employer Partner postings 2026 PW Competitive Funding Program Already secured an unpaid or low paying internship and need additional funds? Consider applying here . Handshake Make sure your profile preferences and career interests are up to date to inform the algorithms See a few other starter search engines below: REU (Research for Undergrads) Inroads (Diversity Focused) LinkedIn WayUp (Finance Internship Examples) Already have a summer internship and need financial support? PW 2026 Internship Competitive Funding Eligibility: Bates sophomores (2028) and juniors (2027) who have received an offer for an unpaid or low-paying internship will be eligible to apply for funds. To apply for Purposeful Work 2026 Competitive Internship Funding you must submit all materials (resume reviewed by PW, short answers, budget and employer verification form) by the Funding Application deadlines (March 1, 2026, April 1, 2026, and end of April 2026) Funding Amounts : Internship funding awards will range from $2500 to $5000 to support internships ranging from 250 to 300 hours. A thoughtful application and budget will be very helpful for the committee’s consideration. Click here for t https://bates.joinhandshake.com/edu/jobs/10879203 he application form on Handshake *Please note- each round has a new application link on Handshake. Purpose Through the Purposeful Work Internship Programs, students explore interests, deepen skills, and build networks during the summer. Students learn about and experience preparation for the overall process of life and work exploration. Approach The Purposeful Work approach to summer internships gives students the tools they need to deepen what they learn through their internship, as well as access to Bates-specific paid internships with employer partners in diverse industries and locations, and the chance to apply for a summer stipend for any unpaid or low-paying internship. Benefits Through the programs, students benefit from application feedback, goal setting, and reflection activities designed to help maximize their experiences, strengthen their skills, and build connections within their site and across industries. After an enriching and reflective experience, students return to campus ready to connect their summer experience to their studies and present on what they’ve learned during their time in a professional environment. Components of the program include: Comprehensive and personalized learning experience Career Counseling that will help strengthen application materials through the Bates Center for Purposeful Work Participation in weekly virtual cohorts to encourage reflection and discussion of personalized goals with fellow Bates students Post-program presentations to reflect on their summer experience and pay their knowledge forward. PW Intern Insights Internship FAQs Quick Links: Bates Summer Funding Opportunities Budget Template Competitive Funding Details Cost of Living Estimator Housing Resources PW 2026 Employer Partner postings Questions? Email purposefulworkinternships@bates.edu . Drop-In Hours & Schedule an Appointment Resume Guide and Cover Letter Guide If you would like to learn more about others’ experiences, please follow us on Instagram @batespurposefulwork and then check out our Instagram Highlights here! Center for Purposeful Work Search these pages Bates Center for Purposeful Work 56 Campus Ave Chase Hall, Suite 101 Lewiston, Maine 04240 PHONE 1-207-786-6232 Email purposefulwork@bates.edu News & Updates September 4, 2026 AESOP trips encourage authenticity, connection The Class of 2030, the third largest in Bates history, gathered to kick off AESOP on Friday, Aug. 28 — the day after move-in day. September 4, 2026 Opening Convocation at Bates welcomes Class of 2030, encourag… The college welcomed the Class of 2030 and new transfer students to the official start of the new academic year at the Sept.  1 Convocation on the Historic Quad. September 4, 2026 Bates welcomes (more) new faculty Bates News began introducing new faculty last week and will continue over the next few weeks. Read our second installment below. Bates\n\t\t\t\t\tCollege 2 Andrews Road Lewiston, Maine 04240 Phone: 1-207-786-6255 Make a Gift Campus Safety Communications Directory Employment Sexual Respect / Title\n\t\t\t\t\t\tIX A-Z Index Privacy Policy Questions &\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFeedback Virtual Tour Previous Next"
