Graduation Outcomes Class of 2020 Post Graduation Outcomes Student Affairs Center for Purposeful Work Opportunities For Students: Recruiting at Bates For Students: Recruiting at Bates The Bates Center for Purposeful Work strives to prepare students for the rigors, realities, and rewards of a meaningful career. We partner with employers of all sizes, from small nonprofits to multinational corporations, to match their needs to the skills and abilities of our students. Throughout the academic year, we invite employers for info sessions , panels, workshops, interviews, and other related events. We collaborate regularly with our colleagues at Bowdoin and Colby, as well across NESCAC and LACN schools, on joint recruitment activities and efforts to highlight what students from the top liberal arts schools in Maine and across New England and the country have to offer. We require all students who participate in campus recruiting activities to abide by our recruiting expectations, guidelines, and policies . We expect Bates students to conduct themselves professionally at all times during recruitment events and activities. If you have any questions about recruiting policies and/or professional conduct, please consult with a Bates Center for Purposeful Work staff member. PW Quick Links Where We Are & Drop In Hours Schedule an Appointment Handshake RAIN Employer Info Session Schedule Cover Letter Guide Resume Guide Center for Purposeful Work Search these pages Bates Center for Purposeful Work 56 Campus Ave Chase Hall, Suite 101 Lewiston, Maine 04240 PHONE 1-207-786-6232 Email purposefulwork@bates.edu News & Updates September 4, 2026 AESOP trips encourage authenticity, connection The Class of 2030, the third largest in Bates history, gathered to kick off AESOP on Friday, Aug. 28 — the day after move-in day. September 4, 2026 Opening Convocation at Bates welcomes Class of 2030, encourag… The college welcomed the Class of 2030 and new transfer students to the official start of the 