    "https://www.bates.edu/purposeful-work/stem-and-pre-health-support-resources/": {
      "title": "STEM and Pre-Health Support & Resources",
      "description": "STEM and Pre-Health Support & Resources | Center for Purposeful Work | Bates College Menu Search Admission Visit Campus Visit Virtually Student Financial Services Academics Calendar Course Catalog Resources Campus Dining Menu Events Map Alumni Alumni Directory Events Reunion Arts Athletics New Students Library News Parents & Families Strategic Planning About Us Purposeful Work College Store Community-Engaged Learning Equity & Inclusion President Sustainability Support Bates The Quad Center for Purposeful Work Opportunities and Programs Page Menu Purpose Connect Where to Find Us Staff Team Make an Appointment Student Teams Purpose and Your Club PW Weekly Newsletters For Alumni and Parents In The News Media Professionals Media Inquiries Prepare Resume, Cover Letter, Interview & Networking Activities to Explore Purposeful Work Professional Development Opportunities Mini Grant Funding Request Form Life After Bates Explore Job Shadow Program Self Assessments Industry Roadshows Spotlights on Alumni Career Paths Purposeful Work Unplugged Curriculum Practitioner-Taught Courses Purposeful Work Infusion Project Faculty Resources for Purposeful Work Infusion Courses Life Architecture Short Term Course First-Year Seminar: Purpose, Work, and College Opportunities Handshake Internship/Job Search Platform Purposeful Work Internships For Employers: Recruiting at Bates For Students: Recruiting at Bates Employer Recruitment Session Schedule Micro-Internships Grants, Credit & Fellowships Industry Specifics STEM and Pre-Health Support & Resources Pre-Law Support & Resources Pre-Business Support & Resources Pre-Engineering Support & Resources Discover Entrepreneurship Application Deadlines by Industry Graduate Support Graduate School Support & Resources Graduate/Professional School Events Outcomes Postgraduation Survey for Class of 2026 Class of 2024 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2023 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2022 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2021 Post Graduation Outcomes Class of 2020 Post Graduation Outcomes Student Affairs Center for Purposeful Work Industry Specifics STEM and Pre-Health Support & Resources STEM and Pre-Health Support & Resources Bates offers a wide range of resources to support your academic, co-curricular, and professional exploration for healthcare and STEM careers. Exploration is an important part of your search for work that is purposeful, whether you have dreamt of being a physician or astronaut since middle school, or are just starting to wonder how to align your interests, strengths, and work. To help you access the appropriate resources on campus, tell us what you’re wondering about: What options exist if I’m interested in STEM but not necessarily healthcare? We advise that you start the exploration process by meeting with Molly Holmberg Brown at Purposeful Work. Lea can help you think through your personal and professional priorities, explore a range of opportunities, and make decisions that align with your interests, strengths, and values. Make an appointment with Molly to dive into your specific interests. What classes should I take if I’m interested in STEM? For assistance with course selection, AP credits, and other course-related questions, your academic advisor is your key faculty contact. Make an appointment with them to dive into your specific questions. In addition, the Recommended Entry Courses webpage highlights introductory courses for each department, program, and major. What classes should I take if I’m interested in healthcare? For assistance with course selection, AP credits, and other course-related questions, Bruno Salazar-Perea is your key faculty contact. Check out these resources to get started. Make an appointment with Bruno to dive into your specific questions. In addition, the Recommended Entry Courses webpage highlights introductory courses for each department, program, and major. How can I explore pre-health, and what opportunities are available for me to gain experience in healthcare and STEM while at Bates? Whether you’re engaging with student groups, job shadows, or the Harward Center during the academic year; or tackling internships, research, and other summer opportunities; there are endless ways for you to find your purpose and meaning. Check out the Gain Experience page to get started. Make an appointment with Molly Holmberg Brown in Purposeful Work to dive into your specific interests. I’m committed to applying for graduate/professional school for healthcare careers. What are my next steps? Regardless of what degree or program you’re considering, Bruno Salazar-Perea is your key faculty contact. Check out these resources to get started. Make an appointment with Bruno to dive into your specific questions. I’m committed to applying for graduate/professional school for STEM careers. What are my next steps? Regardless of what degree or program you’re considering, Molly Holmberg Brown is your key contact and Allen Delong is available from Purposeful Work. Make an appointment with Molly or Allen to dive into your specific questions. PW Quick Links Where We Are & Drop In Hours Schedule an Appointment Handshake RAIN Employer Info Session Schedule Cover Letter Guide Resume Guide Center for Purposeful Work Search these pages Bates Center for Purposeful Work 56 Campus Ave Chase Hall, Suite 101 Lewiston, Maine 04240 PHONE 1-207-786-6232 Email purposefulwork@bates.edu News & Updates September 4, 2026 AESOP trips encourage authenticity, connection The Class of 2030, the third largest in Bates history, gathered to kick off AESOP on Friday, Aug. 28 — the day after move-in day. September 4, 2026 Opening Convocation at Bates welcomes Class of 2030, encourag… The college welcomed the Class of 2030 and new transfer students to the official start of the new academic year at the Sept.  1 Convocation on the Historic Quad. September 4, 2026 Bates welcomes (more) new faculty Bates News began introducing new faculty last week and will continue over the next few weeks. Read our second installment below. Bates\n\t\t\t\t\tCollege 2 Andrews Road Lewiston, Maine 04240 Phone: 1-207-786-6255 Make a Gift Campus Safety Communications Directory Employment Sexual Respect / Title\n\t\t\t\t\t\tIX A-Z Index Privacy Policy Questions &\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFeedback Virtual Tour Previous Next"
