t Graduation Outcomes Class of 2020 Post Graduation Outcomes Student Affairs Center for Purposeful Work Industry Specifics Pre-Engineering Support & Resources Pre-Engineering Support & Resources For current students interested in careers in engineering, Bates offers joint degree programs with a number of prestigious engineering schools, specifically: Columbia, Case Western Reserve, Dartmouth, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute, and Washington University in St. Louis. With the Engineering Combined Plan , students spend three years at Bates taking general education requirements and basic courses in mathematics, physics, and other relevant sciences, before matriculation at the engineering school for concentration in their area of interest for two years. This 3-2 liberal arts/engineering program results in two baccalaureate degrees — one from Bates and one from the specific engineering school. For more information on joint degree options, please check out detailed information provided by the Physics & Astronomy department and contact Professor Ryan Cole ( rcole@bates.edu ) for an appointment to discuss your interests. Center for Purposeful Work Search these pages Bates Center for Purposeful Work 56 Campus Ave Chase Hall, Suite 101 Lewiston, Maine 04240 PHONE 1-207-786-6232 Email purposefulwork@bates.edu News & Updates September 4, 2026 AESOP trips encourage authenticity, connection The Class of 2030, the third largest in Bates history, gathered to kick off AESOP on Friday, Aug. 28 — the day after move-in day. September 4, 2026 Opening Convocation at Bates welcomes Class of 2030, encourag… The college welcomed the Class of 2030 and new transfer students to the official start of the new academic year at the Sept.  1 Convocation on the Historic Quad. September 4, 2026 Bates welcomes (more) new faculty Bates News began introducing new faculty last week and will continue over the next few weeks. Read our second installment below. Bates\n\t\t\t\t\tCollege 2 Andrews Road Lewisto