Graduation Outcomes Class of 2020 Post Graduation Outcomes Student Affairs Center for Purposeful Work Industry Specifics Application Deadlines by Industry Application Deadlines by Industry NOTE: These are very general application deadline ranges. Larger organizations, and corporate entities with more competitive and/or structured programs, tend to recruit earlier, while smaller/mid-size organizations and other industries — that are more budget-based and -dependent — tend to recruit later. ADVICE: Some application periods may be a matter of weeks, while others may be a matter of months. Some recruiters may review applications in batches, while others may do so after their deadlines. Some companies may even close application portals early — unexpectedly and without notice — if they’ve received enough applications. That said, it’s in your best interest to submit applications as soon as you’re ready — don’t wait until deadlines are imminent, especially if you might run into technical difficulties. ARTS Internship: January-June Senior Full-Time: January-June COMMUNICATIONS/MEDIA Internship: September-June Senior Full-Time: October-May CONSULTING First-Year/Sophomore Internship: Very limited (keep a lookout on Handshake, LinkedIn & company careers pages) Junior Internship: Most competitive (especially management/strategy) – Spring of Sophomore Year-September of Junior Year Junior Internship: General – October-April Senior Full-Time: Most Competitive – June-September Senior Full-Time: General – October-April CONSUMER PRODUCTS/GOODS Internship: Most competitive – Spring of Previous Year-October Internship: General – October-April Senior Full-Time: Most competitive – August-March Senior Full-Time: General – August-May EDUCATION Internship: February-June Senior Full-Time: August-June ENVIRONMENT/SUSTAINABILITY Internship: January-June Senior Full-Time: January-June FINANCE First-Year/Sophomore Internship: Very limited (keep a lookout on Handshake, LinkedIn & company careers pages) Junior Internship: Most competitive (especially investment banking) – Spring of Sophomore Year-November of Junior Year Junior Internship: General – Spring of Sophomore Year-April of Junior Year Senior Full-Time: Most competitive – Spring of Junior Year-December of Senior Year Senior Full-Time: General – Spring of Junior Year-May of Senior Year GOVERNMENT/POLITICS Internship: November-June Senior Full-Time: September-March HEALTHCARE (HOSPITALS) Internship: November-March Senior Full-Time: September-June HEALTHCARE (BIOTECH/PHARMA) Internship: October-April Senior Full-Time: September-May INSURANCE/ACTUARY Internship: September-May Senior Full-Time: September-June LEGAL/POLICY/THINK TANKS Internship: August-May Senior Full-Time: September-May MARKETING Internship: August-June Senior Full-Time: October-May NON-PROFIT/NGO Internship: November-May Senior Full-Time: January-June Americorps, City Year, etc.: October-June REAL ESTATE Internship: September-May Senior Full-Time: September-June RECREATION/SPORTS/OUTDOORS Internship: October-June Senior Full-Time: October-June SCIENTIFIC R&D Internship: November-April Senior Full-Time: November-May SOCIAL SERVICES Internship: October-April Senior Full-Time: February-April TECHNOLOGY Internship: September-May Senior Full-Time: October-April PW Quick Links Where We Are & Drop In Hours Schedule an Appointment Handshake RAIN Employer Info Session Schedule Cover Letter Guide Resume Guide Center for Purposeful Work Search these pages Bates Center for Purposeful Work 56 Campus Ave Chase Hall, Suite 101 Lewiston, Maine 04240 PHONE 1-207-786-6232 Email purposefulwork@bates.edu News & Updates September 4, 2026 AESOP trips encourage authenticity, connection The Class of 2030, the third largest in Bates history, gathered to kick off AESOP on Friday, Aug. 28 — the day after move-in day. September 4, 2026 Opening Convocation at Bates welcomes Class of 2030, encourag… The college welcomed the Class of 2030 and new transfer students to 