icine Noorda College of Osteopathic Medicine Boston University Henry M. Goldman School of Dental Medicine New York University College of Dentistry Colorado State University Veterinary Teaching Hospital Tufts University Cummings School of Veterinary Medicine 100% of seniors (5 of 5) applying from the Class of 2023 were accepted to one or more law schools* 88% of alumni (22 of 25) who applied in 2022–23 were admitted to at least one law school* Law School In the 2022–23 admission cycle, alumni matriculated at the following law schools: Harvard Law School, University of Pennsylvania Carey Law School, New York University Law School, University of Virginia School of Law, University of Michigan Law School, Duke University School of Law, Northwestern Pritzker School of Law, Boston University School of Law, Boston College Law School, Fordham University School of Law, Northeastern University School of Law, and Case Western Reserve University School of Law. *Not all applicants worked with the prelaw advisor. Final data on the applicants from 2023-24 will be available from the Law School Admission Council later in 2024. TOP FIELDS AND COMPANIES Our graduates find success in many fields and industries, supported always by the education and experience they received at Bates. Top 10 companies on LinkedIn for Bates graduates Fidelity Investments Boston Children’s Hospital Massachusetts General Hospital Harvard University Liberty Mutual Insurance Google Amazon Harvard Medical School Analysis Group Wellington Management Top fields on LinkedIn for Bates graduates Business Development Education Operations Community and Social Services Healthcare Services Research Media and Communications Finance Sales Legal Information Technology Marketing INTERNSHIPS Kayla graduated with a major in politics and is currently working at Success Academy as a kindergarten teacher in Brooklyn, NY. Kayla Bridgeman ’23 Interned with the LA Maples in Lewiston, Maine. “Purposeful Work has allowed me to explore many avenues of curiosity that I otherwise would not have been able to experience. The PW team offered me a space to reflect on my experiences while uncovering my professional personality. I appreciate their dedication to go the extra mile to provide meaningful support and guidance!” Adilene graduated with a double major in environmental studies and sociology. She received a 2023–24 Watson Fellowship for her project “Weaving Together Activism and Healing.” Adilene Sandoval ’23 Interned with Engage Globally (remote) in Ghana, Africa. “Purposeful Work at Bates has taught me that aligning my passions with my actions brings both joy and empowerment, guiding me towards pursuing my dreams with self-trust. I can not thank PW enough for emphasizing and normalizing the value of exploration without fear but rather curiosity.” Center for Purposeful Work Search these pages Bates Center for Purposeful Work 56 Campus Ave Chase Hall, Suite 101 Lewiston, Maine 04240 PHONE 1-207-786-6232 Email purposefulwork@bates.edu News & Updates September 4, 2026 AESOP trips encourage authenticity, connection The Class of 2030, the third largest in Bates history, gathered to kick off AESOP on Friday, Aug. 28 — the day after move-in day. September 4, 2026 Opening Convocation at Bates welcomes Class of 2030, encourag… The college welcomed the Class of 2030 and new transfer students to the official start of the new academic year at the Sept.  1 Convocation on the Historic Quad. September 4, 2026 Bates welcomes (more) new faculty Bates News began introducing new faculty last week and will continue over the next few weeks. Read our second installment below. Bates\n\t\t\t\t\tCollege 2 Andrews Road Lewiston, Maine 04240 Phone: 1-207-786-6255 Make a Gift Campus Safety Communications Directory Employment Sexual Respect / Title\n\t\t\t\t\t\tIX A-Z Index Privacy Policy Questions &\n\t\t\t\t\t\tFeedback Virtual Tour Previous Next"
